      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`XPUAttentionImpl.forward` called `.contiguous()` on q, k and v before every\r\nflash-attention call:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nq_ = query.contiguous().reshape(bsz * seqlen_q, nheads_q, d)\r\nk_ = key.contiguous().reshape(bsz * seqlen_k, nheads_k, d)\r\nv_ = value.contiguous().reshape(bsz * seqlen_k, nheads_k, d)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn FLUX.2's single-stream blocks q/k/v are head-packed, row-strided *slices* of\r\none fused projection output (`[tokens, 13824]` = `q | k | v | mlp`), so each\r\n`.contiguous()` materialised a fresh `[tokens, heads, 128]` tensor — 3 copies\r\nper block, 144 per DiT forward, 8.8 ms of profiled device time.\r\n\r\nThe sgl-kernel-xpu flash-attention kernel reads rows through their stride, so\r\nthe copies are not needed.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n`multimodal_gen/runtime/layers/attention/backends/xpu_backend.py`: new\r\n`_as_fa_input` helper used for q, k and v. It passes the tensor through\r\nuntouched when the `[rows, heads, head_dim]` view is one the kernel can read\r\ndirectly — unit last-dim stride, heads packed at `head_dim`, row stride a\r\nmultiple of 8, 16-byte-aligned base — and otherwise copies exactly as before.\r\n\r\nThis is XPU-only; no other backend is touched.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nKernel-level probe at the FLUX.2 shape (`[4608, 12, 128]`, token stride 13824):\r\noutput with strided q/k/v is `torch.equal` to output with contiguous inputs.\r\nThe same probe also confirms the kernel accepts a strided *output* buffer and\r\nleaves neighbouring columns untouched (not used by this PR — see follow-up).\r\n\r\n`test_flux2_xpu_norm_fusions.py::test_attention_reads_fused_projection_slices_in_place`\r\n(added here): asserts `_as_fa_input` returns the input's own `data_ptr` for a\r\nfused-projection slice, and that `XPUAttentionImpl.forward` gives a\r\n`torch.equal` result for strided and contiguous inputs. The file is now 6 cases,\r\nall passing on Arc Pro B70.\r\n\r\nEnd to end: no bit-exact fallback warnings; images differ from the parent commit\r\nonly at oneCCL run-to-run noise level (see PR 2).\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nEnd to end (FLUX.2-dev, 1024x1024, 8 steps, bf16, eager, warm, TP4 on 4x\r\nArc Pro B70), 2 runs per side:\r\n\r\n| | denoise (8 steps) | per DiT forward |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| parent commit | 6.140 / 6.129 s | — |\r\n| this commit | 6.077 / 6.095 s | **−6 ms (−0.8%)** |\r\n\r\ntorch.profiler: the 144 `aten::copy_` kernels per forward (8.8 ms) are gone.\r\nFlash attention itself costs ~1.2 ms more per forward with strided reads, so the\r\nnet saving is smaller than the copies removed.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36789285543](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36789285543)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36789285254](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36789285254)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36789285615](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36789285615)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
